 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Set the dashboard's auto-refresh interval to 1m via the top-bar refresh picker (menu list \"Off Auto 5s 10s 30s 1m ...\" → selecting the row labelled \"1 minute\" added \"1m\" to the top bar and to the URL). The save drawer initially showed \"No changes to save\" with {{v5}} disabled (aria-disabled read as \"false\" only after ticking), so I ticked the \"Update default refresh value\" checkbox — this created a \"Changes 1\" tab whose diff showed the addition of + \"refresh\": \"1m\" — and {{v5}} then became enabled; clicking it produced the \"{{v6}}\" toast. Verification: opening Dashboard settings → General, the \"Auto refresh\" field (in this Grafana version the allowed-intervals list, tooltip \"Define the auto refresh intervals that should be available in the auto refresh list\") shows exactly \"5s,10s,30s,1m,5m,15m,30m,1h,2h,1d\". The persisted interval is confirmed by the Settings → JSON Model view, which now contains \"refresh\": \"1m\" (plus \"tags\": [\"bench\"] and \"time\": {\"from\":\"now-6h\",\"to\":\"now\"}), and by reloading the dashboard from a URL with no refresh parameter, after which Grafana rendered the URL as ...&refresh=1m and the top-bar picker reads \"1m\". The dashboard's two panels remain '{{v2}} Notes' (text \"Bench notes for run {{v2}}\") and '{{v2}} Availability'.",
